--------------------------- Changelog -----------------------------

1.0.a - UNRELEASED
Added - Campaign radial menu: hold a hotkey (B or either Ctrl key by default) on the campaign map to open a wheel of abilities at the mouse, move onto one and release the key to use it. Tiles use the game's interface colour and chamfered borders, with narrow gaps between them, and show only icons unless Icons only is turned off. The tile under the mouse lights up in its icon's colour, lifts out of the ring and eases back when you move on. With Tinted tiles on, every usable tile shows a dim tint of its colour at rest. Resting on an ability shows its usual tooltip beside the wheel, F1 included, unless Ability tooltips is turned off. The main wheel has 7 slots by default (1 to 10) and starts with Scavenge, Sustained Burn, Emergency Burn, Transponder, Go Dark, Sensor Burst and Interdiction Pulse, clockwise from the top. Hold the left mouse button on a slot for half a second to give it another of your fleet's abilities, empty it, or make it a submenu with its own icon and colour. Moving onto a submenu extends its tiles at once on an outer ring in that direction; move outward onto one to pick it, or back to the main ring or the center to close it. Submenus hold 5 abilities by default (1 to 10) and cannot contain another submenu. Abilities your fleet lacks or cannot use right now are greyed out, a cooling ability's sector fills from the outer edge inward until it is ready, and active ones pulse. It plays the game's standard interface sounds. Release in the center or outside the ring, or press Escape, to cancel. With Select by direction on, the wheel picks the tile in the mouse's direction however far out the mouse is, like a weapon wheel in a shooter, and only the center or Escape cancels
Note - Requires LunaLib. Change or clear the hotkeys under Hotkeys, the slot counts, Icons only, Tinted tiles, Ability tooltips and Select by direction under Wheel, and the lift and animations under Animation, in LunaLib's mod settings
Note - Your wheel layout is saved for every campaign. data/config/radial_menu.json only sets the starting abilities
